# OSCREATE PLUGIN - building the content of an image
#
#        one defined method is mandatory:
#        - create  responsible for having the image's content built. returns
#                  <True|False>,"message",<built|accepted> - 'built' when the content is on
#                  disk by the time it returns, 'accepted' when a builder has taken the job
#                  and will call the pack route itself when it is done. A plugin returning
#                  only <True|False>,"message" is read as 'accepted'.
#
#        one method is optional:
#        - cancel  stops a build that a builder took and has not finished. returns
#                  <True|False>,"message", False when this plugin holds no such build. The
#                  builder ends the build's stream, so cancel writes nothing to it. A plugin
#                  without it leaves 'luna osimage cancel' answering for a pack only.

# Plugin selection based on the following search path and priority:
#
# 1 osimage name              e.g. plugins/osimage/operations/create/compute.py
# 2 distribution              e.g. plugins/osimage/operations/create/redhat.py
# 3 osrelease                 e.g. plugins/osimage/operations/create/9.py
# 4 default                   e.g. plugins/osimage/operations/create/default.py
